#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064023 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Position of a Particle Given Its Velocity and Initial Position"}] :question/id #uuid "442b883a-d22b-5dda-8f8a-9eead6ae94b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-566" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t) = 2t+3t^2$, where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=1$ when $t=0$, calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$." :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t) &= ∫v(t)dt \\\\\n&= ∫(2t + 3t^{2})dt \\\\\n&= t^{2} + t^{3} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(0) = 1$. Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 &= (0)^{2} + (0)^{3} + C \\\\\nC &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nx(t) = t^3+t^2+1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064024 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43e68991-37f0-543e-a4da-b78b395a8494" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Position of a Particle Given Its Acceleration, Initial Velocity and Initial Position"}] :question/id #uuid "aaa51bb9-cde1-5062-ac75-0f35d6af1f53" :question/math-academy-id "e-567" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t) = 1-2t$, where $t\\geq 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=1$ and velocity $v=2$ when $t=1$, calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t >0$." :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(t) &= ∫a(t)dt \\\\\n&= ∫(1 - 2t)dt \\\\\n&= t - t^{2} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1) = 2$. Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 &= (1) - (1)^{2} + C \\\\\nC &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by\n\n$$\nv(t) = t-t^2 + 2\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(t) &= ∫v(t)dt \\\\\n&= ∫(t - t^{2} + 2)dt \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}t^{2} - \\frac{1}{3}t^{3} + 2t + K\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K$, we use the fact that $x(1) = 1$. Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 &= \\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2} - \\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3} + 2(1) + K \\\\\nK &= -\\frac{7}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nx(t) = \\dfrac{1}{2}t^2-\\dfrac{1}{3}t^3 +2t -\\dfrac{7}{6}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Position of a Particle Given Its Velocity and Initial Position"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b03e6f01-2787-5ba3-b97e-73da9aa7f86d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = 3t^{2} + 2t^{3} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063623} {:answer/id #uuid "b733bc2d-eac0-5e54-92dd-93d059dc3760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = 3t^{2} + 2t^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063624} {:answer/id #uuid "dd360ec9-21f4-5c8b-8de8-af522c7b3c18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = 3t^{2} + 2t^{3} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063625} {:answer/id #uuid "e95e542e-8f9b-5637-a4db-90f7c8bea670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = 3t^{2} + 2t^{3} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063626} {:answer/id #uuid "192102b0-c951-54cd-94e7-2a8dce6f617c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = 3t^{2} + 2t^{3} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "192102b0-c951-54cd-94e7-2a8dce6f617c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = 3t^{2} + 2t^{3} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063627} :answer-field/id #uuid "373c48b0-ac00-598b-9c44-85a45cb3d080" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063622}] :question/id #uuid "1d57deba-f2e4-5693-a811-867d6077d98a" :question/math-academy-id "q-7110" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t) = 6t + 6t^{2}$, where $t > 0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x = 2$ when $t = 0$, calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$." :question/requires-calculator true}]}
